[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: API high-level requirements
UID: FMD-HLR-API
VERSION: Issue 1
DATE: 2026-11-20
OPTIONS:
  MARKUP: Markdown

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @flightmd

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Behaviour of the API item (HTTP service, storage, job queue, airframe history, alerts) as seen at its interfaces,
written from the code under `api/` as built. Parents are system requirements (`03-system/system-requirements.sdoc`).
The low-level requirements are in `llr-api.sdoc`, the design in `06-design/lld-api.md`, and the interfaces in
`03-system/icd/icd-http-api.md` and `03-system/icd/icd-storage.md`. Defaults quoted here are the values of
`api/config.py`; every one can be changed by an environment variable of the same name.
<<<

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Upload and analysis

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-API-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Upload a log
STATEMENT: >>>
`POST /analyse` shall take one log as the multipart field `file`, with optional form fields `airframe_label`,
`contribute_to_dataset` (default false) and `planning_brief_sha256` and the optional header `X-Airframe-Token`.
For an accepted upload it shall answer 200 with `report_id` (a new UUID4), `status` `"processing"`,
`estimated_seconds` 20 and `deduplicated` false, keep the bytes in a file under `<data dir>/uploads` and hand the
analysis to the queue. The format shall be taken from the first 4096 bytes of the content; a gzip or zip file is
accepted as `compressed` and left for the engine to unpack.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: api
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-028

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-API-002
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Upload refusals
STATEMENT: >>>
`POST /analyse` shall answer 400 with a `detail` text, and start no analysis, when the file is shorter than 8
bytes, when the format detector does not recognise the content (the detector's own message is returned), when
`airframe_label` is given and is unusable (a slash, a backslash or a control character), or when
`planning_brief_sha256` is not 64 hexadecimal characters.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: api
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-002
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-028

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-API-003
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Upload size limit
STATEMENT: >>>
An upload larger than `MAX_FILE_SIZE_MB` (default 50; 1 MB is 1024 x 1024 bytes) shall be refused with 413 and
the text "File too large. Maximum size is <n>MB.". A request whose `Content-Length` exceeds the limit plus 65536
bytes shall be refused before its body is read; any other oversized file shall be refused while it is copied to
the upload folder, and the partial copy shall be deleted.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: api
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-003
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-033

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-API-004
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Bounded analyses
STATEMENT: >>>
With the in-process queue, at most `MAX_CONCURRENT_ANALYSES` analyses (default 2, never fewer than 1) shall run
at once; further accepted uploads wait in memory. When 100 jobs are already in state `processing` (queued or
running) `POST /analyse` shall answer 503 "Too many analyses in progress. Try again in a minute.". When the job
cannot be handed to the queue it shall be marked failed and the answer shall be 503 "The analysis queue is
unavailable. Try again in a minute.".
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: api
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-API-005
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Same log again within the hour
STATEMENT: >>>
When the SHA-256 of the uploaded bytes, the airframe label (or none) and the planning-brief hash (or none) all
equal those of a job created less than 3600 s earlier that is processing or complete, `POST /analyse` shall
return that job's `report_id` and status with `deduplicated` true and shall not analyse again. This shall not
apply to an upload that contributes to the data set or that claims a new airframe label. A failed job is never
reused.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: api
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-029

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-API-006
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Progress polling
STATEMENT: >>>
`GET /status/{report_id}` shall return `status` (`processing`, `complete` or `failed`), `progress` (integer 0 to
100), `message`, `eta_seconds` (seconds remaining to one decimal while processing and when the engine gave an
estimate, otherwise null) and, for a failed job, `error`. An unknown, expired or malformed identifier shall give
404 "Report not found or expired.".
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: api
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-028

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-API-007
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Report by identifier only
STATEMENT: >>>
`GET /report/{report_id}` shall return the stored report as JSON with the header `X-FlightMD-Schema-Version`;
202 while the analysis is in progress; 422 with the failure text when it failed; 404 when the identifier is
unknown, expired, malformed or its stored report cannot be read. No route shall list reports or uploads. A
report tagged with an airframe is returned to any caller that presents its identifier; no token is asked.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: api
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-028
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-029

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-API-008
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Result of an analysis job
STATEMENT: >>>
A finished analysis shall be stored under the identifier given at upload, carrying the SHA-256 of the uploaded
bytes (the engine's own value wins when it set one) and the planning-brief hash given at upload. A log the
engine rejects shall leave the job failed with the engine's message, with absolute file paths replaced by
`<file>` and cut to 300 characters; any other error shall leave it failed with "Analysis failed because of an
internal error.". The uploaded file shall be deleted when the job ends, whatever the outcome.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: api
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-028
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-024

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-API-009
STATUS: Active
TITLE: A stored report is not changed
STATEMENT: >>>
The API shall write a report's JSON once, when its analysis completes, and shall serve, export, compare and
summarise from that stored text. Tagging, the planning-brief hash and the log hash are applied before the report
is stored; contribution works on a copy. No route and no background task shall alter a stored report; the only
later operation on it is deletion.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test, Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
Tests show that the stored report is what was completed and that late progress updates do not touch a complete
row. That no other statement updates `report_json` is checked by review of every SQL statement in `api/`.
<<<
ALLOCATION: api
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-029
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-035

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-API-010
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Expiry
STATEMENT: >>>
A sweep at start-up and every 600 s after shall delete every complete report with no airframe label and every
failed job (tagged or not) created more than 3600 s before, together with the cached exports of each deleted
report, and shall delete upload files older than 3600 s. A report tagged with an airframe is never expired. A
deleted report shall answer 404 on every route.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test, Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
The expiry of reports and their exports is tested. No test runs the sweep's removal of old upload files or its
600 s period; a review reads `_sweep`, `_remove_old_uploads` and `_cleanup_loop` (LLR-API-008).
<<<
ALLOCATION: api
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-029

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-API-011
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Restart and stalled jobs
STATEMENT: >>>
Job state shall survive a restart of the API. At start-up with the in-process queue every job still processing
shall be marked failed with an error that starts "interrupted:" and every upload file shall be removed; with the
Redis queue both are left for the workers. A processing job whose row has not been updated for 3600 s shall be
marked failed with the same error by the sweep.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No system requirement asks for this. Without it a job cut off by a restart would be reported as processing for
ever and its upload would stay on disk.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: api
DERIVED: Yes
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-028

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Exports, comparison, health and questions

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-API-012
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Exports by report identifier
STATEMENT: >>>
`GET /export/pdf|json|gpx|kml/{report_id}` shall return the finished report as a PDF, as indented JSON (with
`X-FlightMD-Schema-Version`), and its track as GPX and KML, each as an attachment named from the first 8
characters of the identifier. The status rules of HLR-API-007 apply. GPX and KML shall answer 422 when the report
has no track; PDF shall answer 501 when the PDF library is not installed; a failed build shall answer 500 with a
fixed text.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: api
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-022
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-028

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-API-013
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Export cache
STATEMENT: >>>
Each export of a report shall be built once and kept under `<data dir>/exports/<report id>/` in a file named
from the export kind, the report's schema version and the application version, so that a change of either
version causes a rebuild. A cache that cannot be written shall not fail the request. The cache of a report shall
be removed when the report expires.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: api
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-035
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-022

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-API-014
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Compare two reports
STATEMENT: >>>
`GET /diff?a=<id>&b=<id>` shall return, for two different finished reports, a summary of each, the overall score
change (b minus a, 2 decimals), per-module score changes (null where a module was skipped or not assessed in
either), per-metric changes (4 decimals), finding titles present only in a (`resolved`) or only in b (`new`),
and the categories present in both. Equal identifiers shall give 400.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: api
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-028

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-API-015
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Health
STATEMENT: >>>
`GET /health` shall return `status` "ok", `version` (the installed `flightmd-core` package version, or
`0.0.0+local` when the package is not installed), `schema_version` (the report schema default), `ai_configured`,
`uptime_seconds` and `active_jobs` (jobs in state processing).
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: api
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-028

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-API-016
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Questions about a report
STATEMENT: >>>
`POST /ask/{report_id}` shall take a question of 1 to 500 characters about a finished report. With no AI
provider configured it shall return `{"configured": false, "answer": null}` and make no outbound call. With one
configured it shall send the provider only a system instruction, the cleaned question and a cleaned copy of the
report of at most 24000 characters without file name, place name, track, topic list and chart data, and shall
return the provider's text in `answer`. The answer shall not be stored and shall not change the report. A
provider failure shall give a fixed fallback text, not an error.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: api
COMMENT: >>>
PR-023 confirmed: the route does not check offline mode (`FLIGHTMD_OFFLINE`), so with a key configured and
offline mode on it still calls the provider (LLR-API-029).
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-023

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Airframe history

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-API-017
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Airframe claim and token
STATEMENT: >>>
An airframe is named by a label of 1 to 40 characters after trimming. The first accepted write to an unclaimed
label (a tagged upload, a configuration update or a maintenance entry) shall create a random token, return it
once as `airframe_token` and store only its SHA-256. A request refused for another reason shall not consume the
claim. Every later read or write of that airframe shall need the header `X-Airframe-Token`: 401 when it is
missing or the airframe is unclaimed, 403 when it is wrong.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: api
COMMENT: >>>
Partly met. An upload that claims a label and then fails to reach the queue answers 503 without the token, which
leaves the airframe claimed by a token nobody holds (LLR-API-021). A label longer than 40 characters is cut, not
refused (LLR-API-058).
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-030

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-API-018
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Airframe configuration and maintenance
STATEMENT: >>>
`GET` and `PUT /airframe/{label}/config` and `POST /airframe/{label}/maintenance` shall read and change the
pre-flight checklist (at most 50 items of 200 characters), the maintenance interval (above 0 and at most 100000
hours, or null), the alert rules (at most 20), the webhook address and the maintenance log (ISO 8601 date, type
of 1 to 120 characters, notes of at most 2000). A field left out of an update stays; null clears it. Each answer
shall carry the configuration, total flight hours and hours since the last maintenance entry (2 decimals),
`maintenance_due` and `flight_count`, counting each distinct log once.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: api
COMMENT: >>>
Hours since the last maintenance entry count the flights uploaded on or after its date, not those flown after
it (LLR-API-090).
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-030

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-API-019
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Trends
STATEMENT: >>>
`GET /trends/{airframe_label}` shall return, to a holder of the token, every finished report tagged with the
label, oldest upload first and each distinct log once, with report identifier, file name, upload time, overall
score, grade, per-module scores (null for a module skipped or not assessed) and every key metric as
`<analyser>.<name>`.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: api
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-030

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-API-020
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Airframe record
STATEMENT: >>>
`GET /export/airframe/{label}/pdf` shall return, to a holder of the token, a PDF of the airframe's flights
(upload date, file name, duration in minutes, score, grade), its maintenance log, checklist and maintenance
status, as an attachment whose name carries the label, with an ASCII fallback name.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: api
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-030
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-022

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-API-021
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Applied parameter changes and their verification
STATEMENT: >>>
`POST /airframe/{label}/changes` shall record, for a finished report tagged with that airframe, 1 to 50
parameter changes (name, optional old value, new value), who applied them (`user` or `uaop`) and an optional
note. `GET /airframe/{label}/changes` shall list them newest first, each with a verification: `pending` until a
different log is uploaded for the airframe after the change was recorded, then `improved`, `worse`, `mixed` or
`unchanged`, from the findings that name a changed parameter and from score changes of 2.0 points or more, with
the resolved and new finding titles and the score changes. Both routes need the token.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: api
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-031

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Alerts

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-API-022
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Alert rules and webhook
STATEMENT: >>>
When a tagged analysis completes and its airframe has alert rules and a webhook address, the API shall evaluate
each rule (`metric`, `lt` or `gt`, `threshold`) against the new report and, if at least one is breached, send
one HTTP POST to the webhook with a JSON body whose `content` and `text` name the airframe, the report
identifier and each breached rule with its value. A rule whose metric the report does not have is skipped. No
failure of rule evaluation or delivery shall change the outcome of the analysis. A deduplicated upload sends
nothing.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test, Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
Rule evaluation, the call to the sender and the handling of its failures are tested. No test reads the posted
body; a review reads the message building in `send_alert_webhook` (LLR-API-098).
<<<
ALLOCATION: api
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-032

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-API-023
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Webhook address restrictions
STATEMENT: >>>
A webhook address shall be accepted, when saved and again before every send, only if it is at most 2048
characters with no whitespace or control character, uses `https` (or `http` when `ALLOW_HTTP_WEBHOOKS` is true),
names a host, and every address the host resolves to is a public unicast address. The POST shall go to the first
address that was checked, shall not follow redirects, shall time out after 5 s and shall not be retried; only a
2xx answer counts as delivered.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
SYS-032 asks only for the https rule. The address checks are needed because the address is supplied by a user
and the request is made from inside the operator's network.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: api
DERIVED: Yes
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-032

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Abuse protection and observability

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-API-024
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Rate limits and client address
STATEMENT: >>>
The API shall limit, per client address and per hour, `POST /analyse` to `RATE_LIMIT_PER_HOUR` (default 10),
`POST /ask` to `ASK_RATE_LIMIT_PER_HOUR` (default 30) and each of the two PDF routes to `PDF_RATE_LIMIT_PER_HOUR`
(default 30), answering 429 beyond that. The client address shall be the socket peer, unless the peer is inside
`TRUSTED_PROXIES`; then it is the right-most `X-Forwarded-For` entry that is not a trusted proxy. A malformed
`TRUSTED_PROXIES` shall stop the start-up.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test, Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
The client-address rule is tested. No test drives a route past its limit or starts the application with a bad
`TRUSTED_PROXIES`; a review checks the `@limiter.limit` decorators, the limit strings and the call in
`lifespan`.
<<<
ALLOCATION: api
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-033

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-API-025
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Browser origins and request log
STATEMENT: >>>
Cross-origin browser calls shall be allowed from the origins in `CORS_ORIGINS` only, without credentials. Every
response shall carry `X-Request-ID` (12 hexadecimal characters). The API shall log one JSON line per request with
request id, method, route template, status and duration in ms, and never the raw path, client address or file
name.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test, Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
The request id is tested. No test checks the CORS headers or the content of the log line; a review checks the
`CORSMiddleware` arguments and `_log_request`.
<<<
ALLOCATION: api
COMMENT: >>>
A 500 answer for an exception not handled inside the application carries no `X-Request-ID` (LLR-API-002).
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-033

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-API-026
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Metrics
STATEMENT: >>>
`GET /metrics` shall give Prometheus text: HTTP counts and timings by route template, analyses by log format and
outcome, and analysis duration by format. Label values come from fixed sets; no identifier, file name or
position appears. When `METRICS_TOKEN` is set the route shall need `Authorization: Bearer <token>` (401 without,
403 when wrong); when it is empty the route is open. The route is not in the OpenAPI schema.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: api
COMMENT: >>>
With the Redis queue the analysis counters are kept in the worker processes, which serve no `/metrics`
(LLR-API-100).
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-033

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Contributed logs

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-API-027
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Contribution and withdrawal
STATEMENT: >>>
Only when `contribute_to_dataset` is true shall a completed analysis keep the uploaded file and a copy of the
report with `file_name` and `report_id` emptied and `location_name`, `gps_path`, `gps_path_wind_speed_ms` and
`gps_path_hdop` set to null, under a `contribution_id` equal to the first 32 hexadecimal characters of the log's
SHA-256, which the upload answer returns. The same log is stored once. A failure to store shall not fail the
analysis. `DELETE /dataset/{contribution_id}` shall remove the file and the copy and answer 204, or 404 when
there is none. `GET /dataset/stats` shall return the count and total bytes.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: api
COMMENT: >>>
A withdrawal sent while the contributing analysis is still running answers 404 and the contribution is stored
afterwards (LLR-API-025).
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-034

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Storage, queue and configuration

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-API-028
STATUS: Active
TITLE: One data directory and one database
STATEMENT: >>>
The API shall keep everything it stores under the directory `FLIGHTMD_DATA_DIR` (default `data`, relative to the
working directory): the SQLite file `flightmd.db` in WAL mode holding reports with their job state, airframes,
contributions and applied parameter changes; `uploads/`; `exports/`; and `blobs/` unless S3 is configured. The
schema shall be created and brought up to date at first use by numbered migrations, each applied once and
recorded.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: api, deployment
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-035

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-API-029
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Import of earlier stores
STATEMENT: >>>
At start-up the API shall import the JSON stores of earlier versions (`reports/`, `airframes/`,
`training_contributions/`) found under `api/data` or under the data directory into the database and the blob
store, without overwriting rows that already exist, and shall then rename each directory to `<name>.imported` so
it is not imported again. A file that cannot be read shall be logged and left in the renamed directory.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: api, deployment
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-035

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-API-030
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Store for contributed logs
STATEMENT: >>>
Contributed log files shall be kept in `<data dir>/blobs`, or in the S3-compatible bucket `FLIGHTMD_S3_BUCKET`
under `FLIGHTMD_S3_PREFIX` when a bucket is set. Keys are made by the API and shall be refused if they could
name a path outside the store. Setting a bucket without the S3 library installed shall fail with a message
naming the package extra to install.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test
ALLOCATION: api, deployment
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-035
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-034

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-API-031
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Optional Redis queue
STATEMENT: >>>
When `FLIGHTMD_REDIS_URL` is set the API shall hand each analysis to arq workers through Redis instead of
running it in its own process, using the report identifier as the queue job identifier. A worker shall run at
most `MAX_CONCURRENT_ANALYSES` jobs at once, give each 900 s and never retry. Workers share the data directory
with the API. Setting the address without the queue library installed shall fail the hand-over with a message
naming the package extra to install.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No system requirement asks for a second queue. It exists so that more than one API process can run; the limit of
SYS-003 then holds per worker process.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Test, Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
The choice of queue and the missing-library message are tested. No test runs Redis or an arq worker; a review
checks `RedisQueue.submit` and `api/worker.py`.
<<<
ALLOCATION: api, deployment
DERIVED: Yes
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: HLR-API-032
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Configuration
STATEMENT: >>>
The API shall take its settings from environment variables (names not case sensitive) and from a `.env` file at
the repository root, ignoring names it does not know, with the defaults of `api/config.py`: file size 50 MB,
10 uploads, 30 questions and 30 PDFs per hour, 2 concurrent analyses, local development origins, no trusted
proxy, https-only webhooks, data directory `data`, no S3, no Redis, no metrics token, AI provider `groq` with no
key.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No system requirement names the settings. They are stated here because the limits of SYS-003 and SYS-033 and the
directory of SYS-035 take their values from them.
<<<
VERIFICATION: Inspection
VERIFICATION_NOTE: >>>
No test reads the defaults as a set; tests override single settings. A review compares `Settings` with
`.env.example`, `api/render.yaml` and `docker-compose.yml`.
<<<
ALLOCATION: api, deployment
DERIVED: Yes
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-033
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS-035

[[/SECTION]]
